1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting
sun over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,900
kicking a pebble, I leap off like a bear.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,380
Like the joking type, here in Kashiwa,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laugh that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,140
Somewhere, a little good energy.

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
Even as sound, it's the real thing,
the only one that holds.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
With a yawn, the streets that never change

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are even gentler.

9
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,960
the day is already ending, isn't it?

11
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,840
Are there really yakitori stalls here?

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,460
With the pointy hat...

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,600
Leaving people behind on retirement...

14
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,080
The sun is sinking.

15
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow it'll sink and end too, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,720
Even a magazine, laughing, happiness too.

17
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,660
Taking it easy, I realized.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool.

19
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:29,675
So sleepy.

20
00:01:29,725 --> 00:01:34,600
No wonder my eyes are going
blurry after gaming all night.

21
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,680
Whee-sh.

22
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,660
Oops. Wrong room.

23
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:56,140
Where are you going, Ryo-chan?

24
00:01:56,340 --> 00:01:56,980
Reiko?

25
00:01:58,060 --> 00:01:59,720
So this is really the place?

26
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:02,020
So it's the Kameari Park
police box after all.

27
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,840
A police box full of women.

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,440
They've really gone and redecorated it flashily again,
haven't they.

29
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:14,880
Here he comes! Drilla Man!

30
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,780
You didn't have to come.

31
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,000
What did you say!

32
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,020
You're late, Kankichi!

33
00:02:20,460 --> 00:02:21,760
You're totally late.

34
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,380
Sorry, sorry.

35
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:25,980
Why are you here?

36
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:29,160
Anyway, what happened to everyone else?

37
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,920
The Chief's on an overseas
business trip starting today.

38
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,540
I didn't hear about that.

39
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,580
It all came up suddenly.

40
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,840
Terai-san fell down the stairs at
home last night and was hospitalized.

41
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,720
And Nakagawa-san's
company suddenly got busy,

42
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,020
so he'll be taking some time off.

43
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:47,460
No way.

44
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:51,020
If it's just you and me,
it'll hurt our work, you know.

45
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,640
Then why bring these guys in?

46
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:56,940
Don't tell me you two are the ones
who made the police box look like this?

47
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:59,720
We came all the way out here just for you.

48
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,440
Making it a bit more comfortable to work in is only natural,
isn't it?

49
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:04,280
What?

50
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:05,220
What?

51
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:10,200
All right, enough of that.
Let's get to work.

52
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,780
Damn it, what a mess.

53
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:17,420
W-what are you doing, Kankichi?

54
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,100
That's my line.

55
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,640
That's my seat.

56
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:21,660
Don't use it without permission.

57
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:23,460
Is that so?

58
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,860
It was so filthy I
figured no one was using it.

59
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:28,680
No way.

60
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,780
What was in the drawer

61
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,760
was nothing but junk.

62
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,500
That was my collection!

63
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,900
Where was it?

64
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,440
I threw it all away.

65
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:42,600
What?

66
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:47,120
I spent tens of thousands collecting that!

67
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:53,620
Consider this a chance to turn over a
new leaf and get serious about your work.

68
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,500
You don't need a desk anyway, do you?

69
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,700
I use a desk too, you know!

70
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,180
You only use it when
writing reprimand letters!

71
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:01,880
Right.

72
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,240
So

73
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:06,340
This is plenty for your desk.

74
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:10,260
Wow, what a fine mikan crate.

75
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:11,220
What are you doing?

76
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,900
Now that the Chief's not here,

77
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,140
I'm the highest-ranking one here, you know!

78
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:18,940
What are you doing?

79
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:24,880
I came to hang out!

80
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,940
How are you? Let's have some tea.

81
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,640
Here, a little something for you.

82
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,660
Thanks!

83
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,960
Doesn't the floor feel all squishy here?

84
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:35,120
Yeah, it does.

85
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,660
You guys

86
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:41,440
Lucky!

87
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,120
Ahahaha!

88
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,000
Good luck!

89
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:45,320
That energy!

90
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:46,260
Yeah!

91
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:46,920
Yeah!

92
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,660
Yeah!

93
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:51,500
Are you all right, Ryo-chan?

94
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,300
Damn it.

95
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:56,520
Because you were just standing around
spaced out in a place like that.

96
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,960
That's right, that's right.

97
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:58,820
So what?

98
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:04,780
Well, I can't stand being stuck
in a place full of women like this!

99
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,960
Where are you going, Ryo-chan?

100
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,380
I'm going on patrol.

101
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,220
Don't tell me you're just going to slack off,
saying that.

102
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:14,400
He's definitely off to the pachinko parlor.

103
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,700
When I say patrol, it's a patrol!

104
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:19,300
There's a limit to how much you can push it!

105
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,400
This is so boring.

106
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,980
Guess I'll go take a change of scenery.

107
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,980
Wasn't this supposed to be patrol?

108
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,880
Didn't he once say

109
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,920
the Chief asked us to.

110
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:42,020
you'd slack off right away,
so never take your eyes off him.

111
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,140
Damn the Chief, always meddling.

112
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,520
Hey, Mori Yumi is flying in the sky!

113
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,520
What, no way!

114
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:49,500
That's impossible!

115
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:51,300
Look, Kankichi!

116
00:05:57,300 --> 00:06:00,200
I'm not letting them keep
pestering me like this!

117
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,440
That's money!

118
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:07,880
Yes!

119
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:14,040
I'm getting that back.

120
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,120
Flutter.

121
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:16,480
Crunch.

122
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:20,840
Crunch.

123
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:24,360
Falling for such a simple trick.

124
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,340
Yes, I'll patrol properly.

125
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:29,260
This is just walking the dog.

126
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,220
Phew, what a rotten day it's been.

127
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,320
Guess I'll head back and play some games.

128
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,560
Sakonji, play a game with me for a bit.

129
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,960
Sakonji isn't here?

130
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,780
Sakonji's not here.

131
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:52,600
He should be at a judo training
camp down in Izu starting today.

132
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,420
Oh well,
I'll get Honda to play with me, then.

133
00:06:57,420 --> 00:07:01,680
Honda's up in the Tohoku area
giving instruction at Hakubai.

134
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,760
Then how about Hojo?

135
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:08,320
Hojo's holed up at a
hotel for a study session.

136
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,420
Then someone else, then.

137
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:15,900
Most people are on duty or on night shifts,
so there's hardly anyone around.

138
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,520
What?

139
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:33,300
Quit your noise, you two!
You're disturbing my work!

140
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:36,020
Come on, it's break time.

141
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:38,560
You're probably writing a
self-criticism report anyway, right?

142
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,900
I'm writing a report on a lost item.

143
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:49,080
You got the kanji wrong.

144
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,880
Really? I can't believe it.

145
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,900
You two distracted me!

146
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,120
If you want to take a break,
go take it in the break room!

147
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,680
Hey, don't blame me for this.

148
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,440
Why should I take orders from you?

149
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,960
Everyone, the break room is more relaxing.

150
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,020
Okay!

151
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:10,640
Reiko's right!

152
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:11,460
Let's all go!

153
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,280
Bye-bye!

154
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:16,820
Hey, I outrank Reiko, you know!

155
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,380
What a noisy bunch.

156
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,980
That's just what happens
when women get together.

157
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:25,980
It's the same overseas, too.
Girls just love to chat.

158
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,740
Women

159
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:33,860
It suddenly got quiet in here

160
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,300
Yeah, I wonder what's going on.

161
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,500
Somehow, the silence makes me more uneasy.

162
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,520
Like this? Or is it wrong?

163
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,160
It's none of your business.

164
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,300
Sh, sh!

165
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:50,840
Couldn't you at least
tell me what you're doing?

166
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,720
What's this, you're making a bag?

167
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:56,040
I'm weaving it out of paper cord.

168
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,500
I'm having trouble from here on.

169
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,620
Let me take a look.

170
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:02,780
Yeah, I see.

171
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,160
Wh-wait a second

172
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,820
Just watch in silence.

173
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,094
See here,

174
00:09:09,144 --> 00:09:12,400
you reduce the number of stitches like this,

175
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,980
pulling them out one by one,

176
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,160
and then you weave it up.

177
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:22,060
See, the tip naturally tapers in, right?

178
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:23,480
Wow, amazing!

179
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,340
You're really skillful.

180
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:27,780
Here you go.

181
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:28,640
Thanks.

182
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:30,600
Looks like a pro made it.

183
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,640
Hey, how do you make this part?

184
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,100
It's not in the book.

185
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,160
This one's beadwork

186
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,400
A flower is easy.

187
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,400
You know how?

188
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:40,800
Yeah.

189
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,860
Coat the beads with -

190
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:46,872
make a loop, then wrap it around like this,

191
00:09:46,922 --> 00:09:50,800
do it like this and this,
and the aura's complete!

192
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:53,100
Wow! That's amazing!

193
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,800
You can make something like that
with those big clumsy fingers?

194
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:58,960
Ryo-chan basically loves crafts, you know.

195
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,140
Could you take a look at this one too?

196
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,060
Hey.

197
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:06,850
Who'd have thought a caveman
could do something like that,

198
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,020
he's not one to underestimate.

199
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,920
Shall we have lunch soon?

200
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:17,320
Agreed.

201
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:20,600
Now, what should we get today?

202
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,200
I brought bento boxes.

203
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,600
Let's eat together.

204
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,080
Of course.

205
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:30,780
Here he comes again.

206
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,220
There's one for Ryo-san too.

207
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,340
S-so much?

208
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,960
Because you helped us out
with so many things yesterday.

209
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,280
Well, it's kind of like this...

210
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:49,600
Sensei, eat this!

211
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,000
Itadakimasu!

212
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:56,260
I feel like a girls' school teacher.

213
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:59,200
Well then, itadakimasu!

214
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,200
It's delicious!

215
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:01,880
Really!

216
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:03,140
Try this one!

217
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:03,920
Thank you!

218
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:05,800
This is delicious!

219
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:08,240
How did you make it?

220
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:11,960
Is it good, Ryotsu-san?

221
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:15,180
Could you teach us the
rest of today's lesson?

222
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:16,100
Sure.

223
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,380
Gutta-gutta

224
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:22,540
Reiko-san,

225
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,400
we're making a dessert,

226
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:28,460
but we can't decorate it
nicely like the picture.

227
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:31,680
This is a bit tricky, isn't it?

228
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:33,020
Let's see, let's see.

229
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:36,340
I've made this before.

230
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:38,440
I'll make it for you.

231
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:40,360
There we go, I guess.

232
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:44,500
Hey, it's so incredibly delicious,
I can't believe it!

233
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:51,500
How can you make something like this? The last
time I taught the two of them how to make desserts,

234
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:56,680
they mastered it in no time. If you have the ingredients,
I'll make you more.

235
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,160
Just watch, will you? Well, you'll see.

236
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:02,840
Here you go.

237
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,700
Aaaah!

238
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:07,720
Pretty.

239
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,860
Prettier than in Japan.

240
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:12,300
Your fruit cutting is really impressive,
isn't it?

241
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,500
This guy's knife work is

242
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,160
rarely praised by anyone.

243
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,180
My grandma always praised him, you know.

244
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:22,080
He's surprisingly good at everything.

245
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,220
Except for work, though.

246
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,160
Mind your own business.

247
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,460
Hahaha.

248
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,900
Wow, how pretty!

249
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:46,020
That looks delicious.

250
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:49,240
I got the ingredients from Kanda Sushi,
you know.

251
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:50,840
Let's trade.

252
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:53,820
Go ahead. I made extra, so.

253
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,740
Me too, me too, me too!

254
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,660
Here you go, eat up!

255
00:12:57,660 --> 00:12:59,160
Which one should I pick?

256
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,660
He's really settled in lately

257
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:03,920
Isn't that a good thing?

258
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,180
There, it's done.

259
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,780
Wow, how pretty.

260
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,720
Next, mine too, please.

261
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:17,200
Yay, finished!

262
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:20,640
It's already done?
A handmade one-piece dress!

263
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:23,560
Yeah, I thought it would take a bit longer.

264
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:26,560
That's because my teaching was good,
you know.

265
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:29,980
Yes, yes, we're grateful to Kankichi.

266
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:31,620
Kankichi, of all people...

267
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:35,320
Until now, you never even
called me by my name properly.

268
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,400
Hey, come over here and show me quickly.

269
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:37,960
Mm.

270
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,260
Wait, hold on, Komachi.

271
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,760
That's not good, is it?
Right in front of me.

272
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:57,000
No way!
If you were here, you should have said so.

273
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:58,380
I've been here the whole time.

274
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:00,320
Ugh, just get out already.

275
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,380
I know, I know.

276
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:04,580
Honestly, Komachi, you're such a klutz.

277
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:10,200
Before, it definitely wouldn't have ended with just laughs,
I'd think,

278
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:11,300
right?

279
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:19,740
You know, Kankichi...

280
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:23,460
If he were a woman,
he'd make such a good wife, don't you think?

281
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:33,380
Hey, what are you suddenly saying,
Komachi-chan?

282
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:35,660
Yeah, what are you thinking?

283
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:39,860
But he's good at cooking,
and he can do handicrafts and sewing too.

284
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,100
And he's good at shopping, too.

285
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:44,340
He always gets good stuff cheap.

286
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:45,300
Right?

287
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:46,940
Even Matoi-chan?

288
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:49,540
You two are forgetting
the most important thing.

289
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:53,220
I'm bad at cleaning and laundry.

290
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,700
You've seen my room, right?

291
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,040
That's right.

292
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:03,320
But lately, more and more women
can't clean or do laundry either.

293
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,820
Like that garbage house they showed on TV?

294
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:08,500
Kankichi isn't that bad, is he?

295
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:09,940
How ridiculous.

296
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:14,140
I've been wondering since earlier,
what are you making?

297
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:18,260
It's a tablecloth.

298
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:21,020
It'd be good to have one when
we all eat together, right?

299
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:24,120
Honestly,
what you're doing is basically wife's work!

300
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,040
W-what?

301
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:30,120
The only problem is how it looks.

302
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,740
Want to try some makeup?

303
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:40,980
Let's do it.

304
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:45,380
Hey, you two aren't seriously going to...?

305
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,420
Don't worry, leave it to me.

306
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,400
H-hey, stop that!

307
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:54,420
Put the foundation on good and thick.

308
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:56,380
We should add some eyeshadow too.

309
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:00,920
Please, stop.

310
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,940
I wonder if that's enough.

311
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:12,400
What the heck is going on?

312
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,100
What is this?

313
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:18,440
That's - !

314
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:22,580
Sorry, sorry! Your face is so strong
that I went overboard with the makeup.

315
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:23,980
Please, let me try again!

316
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:29,520
For Ryo-san, those thick eyebrows
are the problem, aren't they?

317
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,512
And your eyes look scary,

318
00:16:31,562 --> 00:16:34,120
so it'd be better to give you
double eyelids for a gentler look.

319
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,900
Let's shave off that stubble too.

320
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,480
Looks like we can make it work.

321
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,300
How's this?

322
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:52,420
This is Ryo-san

323
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:54,000
He looks totally different.

324
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,060
Way better than before.

325
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,320
This is

326
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:00,820
me.

327
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:10,120
I thought you were seriously reading a book,

328
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,760
but it's a fashion magazine.

329
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:15,060
Well, makeup really is deep
when you look at it like this.

330
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:16,300
I'm back.

331
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:17,880
Welcome back.

332
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:18,800
Welcome back.

333
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:20,340
I bought something.

334
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,280
The cosmetics you asked for.

335
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,400
Thanks!

336
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,440
And I also got this at the store,

337
00:17:27,260 --> 00:17:30,560
apparently there's a new cosmetics
launch event in Ginza today.

338
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:32,340
Right, let's go check it out then.

339
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,780
Hurry up, let's go!

340
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:38,560
Kankichi's completely hooked on this

341
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,440
I have a bad feeling about this.

342
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:48,220
I've been studying makeup on
my own these past few days.

343
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:51,520
I thought I'd show you the results today.

344
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:57,500
Ryo-chan, you've completely
started talking like a woman.

345
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:01,060
So why am I the guinea pig here?

346
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:03,320
You never wear makeup normally, do you?

347
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:05,180
Leave it to me.

348
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:06,740
Here we go.

349
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:22,260
How do I look?

350
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:27,820
Wow, Mato-chan!

351
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:29,620
I never thought I'd turn out this beautiful.

352
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:31,100
It's like magic.

353
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,340
Is that really me?

354
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:35,560
Teach me next time.

355
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,600
Me too.

356
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:37,360
Me too.

357
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:38,220
Hey,

358
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:40,520
Kankichi did this for you two,

359
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,500
We didn't study makeup for its own sake,
you know.

360
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:44,700
Have you forgotten the original purpose?

361
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:46,500
Right.

362
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:49,080
It's to make someone beautiful.

363
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:52,860
Komachi's already a beauty,
so it's not much work for her.

364
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:56,300
But in my case,
it's not that simple, so it's tough.

365
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:59,140
Don't worry, you'll definitely manage.

366
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:00,360
Because we'll help you.

367
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,220
We'll help you too.

368
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:07,020
Thanks, everyone.

369
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:10,000
I've got a feeling something's wrong.

370
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:21,440
A gorilla, did you say?

371
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:25,960
Yes, a gorilla in transit escaped and is holed up in an apartment unit,
apparently.

372
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:28,380
Understood. I'll handle it right away.

373
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:32,260
Time for that man to step up.

374
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:38,460
Is Ryotsu here?

375
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:40,000
Boss.

376
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,160
Kankichi's in the back, though.

377
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,580
It's an incident! Get moving right away!

378
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,340
Yeah, but...

379
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:49,620
Call him in right away.

380
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:51,600
Yes, well then.

381
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,840
Ready, go... Kan-chan!

382
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:55,960
K-Kan-chan?

383
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,860
Here you are, sorry for the wait!

384
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,840
Long time no see! It's been ages.

385
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:02,340
Hehe.

386
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:04,500
R-Ryotsu... is that you?

387
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:05,460
Yes.

388
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:06,880
Woooah!

389
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,460
Hey, that's impossible.

390
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:15,100
Shut up! Whether it's impossible or not,

391
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:17,180
you have to do it.

392
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,960
Hurry up and go catch
that gorilla over there.

393
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,500
Me alone?

394
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:24,040
Of course.

395
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,280
But... that's too much.

396
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,000
That's cruel.

397
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,940
Putting Kan-chan alone in such danger?

398
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,700
I'm a delicate maiden, you know.

399
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:35,780
Even if he's a man,

400
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:39,420
Ryo-chan is now a woman
in both body and mind.

401
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,980
I don't think that's possible, though.

402
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:42,580
Then what should we do?

403
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:43,900
How about it?

404
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,500
Somebody help!

405
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,200
Little one.

406
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:48,980
That's right.

407
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:52,640
Apparently there's a
three-month-old baby in that room.

408
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,800
So we can't use tear gas
grenades or anything like that.

409
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,300
Someone has to rush in and rescue them.

410
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,060
They're apparently asleep right now,

411
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,600
but if they wake up and start crying...

412
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:04,960
Somebody help!

413
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:09,780
I'll do it.

414
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:11,740
Can you handle it, Ryotsu?

415
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:12,480
Yes.

416
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:12,640
Yes!

417
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:17,180
As a woman, I can't just abandon a baby.

418
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:20,240
My maternal instincts are aching!

419
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:22,740
I'm going!

420
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:25,640
Komachi, Naoko, count on you to back me up!

421
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:26,460
Yeah!

422
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:34,200
Okay.

423
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:36,700
Okay.

424
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:39,490
Alright,

425
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:42,380
Good girl.

426
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,820
Uh-oh, she's starting to cry.

427
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:49,880
This is getting dangerous!

428
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,960
There, there,
we have to get out of here fast.

429
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:09,460
Oh no, what do I do?

430
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:15,040
Tan-chan, over here! Komachi,
hurry up, I'm counting on you! Okay.

431
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,320
Watch out for the gorilla!

432
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:25,920
It's okay, okay!
Come on, Kan-chan, hurry and use it too.

433
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:31,460
No, I'm wearing a skirt! This is no time to be embarrassed,
you know. But...

434
00:22:32,460 --> 00:23:02,440
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...
no, no, no, no, no!

435
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:05,480
Mm, I'm back.

436
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:10,780
Thanks for holding down the fort.
I'm back on duty as of today.

437
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:16,500
Sorry for worrying you all.
Welcome back, everyone. Welcome back!

438
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:24,440
Where's Ryotsu? Come to think of it, I don't see him.
Where'd he go? Right?

439
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,980
Looks like you've become a good bride Ah.

440
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:44,280
I can't take this life anymore!

441
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:46,900
Help me!

442
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:30,820
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets.

443
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:38,340
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

444
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:43,880
Take a turn at that corner over there.

445
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:49,020
You can meet everyone, everyone.

446
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:53,640
Over there, there's Kame-ari.

447
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:57,020
Surely there's Kame-ari.

448
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:02,300
Come on, everyone, to our town.

449
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:06,920
Over there, there's Kame-ari.

450
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:10,180
Surely there's Kame-ari.

451
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:15,400
Come on, everyone, to our town.

452
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:17,000
Thank you.

453
00:25:21,660 --> 00:25:25,720
Lost customers to the shopping street?
We'll win them back in no time.

454
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:28,560
Leave anything to do with
business to this Ryotsu-sama.

455
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:31,740
We'll come up with ideas
that make everyone go "Wow!"

456
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:35,980
Come along next time to the Kameari shopping street,
nice to meet you.

457
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:40,460
Over there is Kameari.

458
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:43,840
Well, surely Kameari.

459
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:49,140
Come on, everyone, to our town.

460
00:25:50,060 --> 00:25:50,740
Thank you.

